ated by dissolving sugar in alcohol, due to differential solubility.</p>\n<p><b>Statement II :</b> Rose essence from rose petals is seperated by steam distillation due to its high volatility and insolubility in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.445ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1964.6 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1186.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>\n","chapter":"practical-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2026-online-6th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i-a-mi-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-jcymuacpkqfy8vz2","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p><b>Statement I :</b> A mixture of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.453ex\" height